From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:16:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Plugins: a value shared with other plugins (share,
 events:shared)

A plugin with the permission "share" can hand other plugins a value:
await a2.share(value) (JSON, up to 64 KB; null withdraws it). Plugins
with "events:shared" hear a2.on("shared", { plugin, value }) at once,
and every value shared so far when they start. What a plugin no longer
loaded shared goes with it. So a pet tracker can tell a map which pets to
show, without either reading the other's data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
